From: meta-odyssey-demo <build@local>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Input: ads7846 - arm nPENIRQ with an X-position bootstrap read

Even with the dummy clearing cycle, the XPT2046 on this panel never asserts
nPENIRQ after probe. Bench tests over spidev showed it only arms when the
last conversion before power-down is an X-position read (0xD0) sent as one
full-duplex transfer - not the Y-position/PWRDOWN the driver's bootstrap
ends on. Replace the probe-time vaux bootstrap with that conversion; the
IRQ-driven sampling path keeps nPENIRQ armed afterwards. Board-specific.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific quirk]

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/ads7846.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/ads7846.c
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/ads7846.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/ads7846.c
@@ -1371,10 +1371,29 @@
 	 * Take a first sample, leaving nPENIRQ active and vREF off; avoid
 	 * the touchscreen, in case it's not connected.
 	 */
-	if (ts->model == 7845)
+	if (ts->model == 7845) {
 		ads7845_read12_ser(dev, PWRDOWN);
-	else
-		(void) ads7846_read12_ser(dev, READ_12BIT_SER(vaux));
+	} else {
+		/*
+		 * This XPT2046 only arms nPENIRQ after a conversion ending on the
+		 * X-position channel, sent as one full-duplex transfer; the default
+		 * Y-position/PWRDOWN bootstrap leaves it unarmed. Do it once at probe.
+		 */
+		{
+			struct ads7846_buf bootstrap = {
+				.cmd = READ_12BIT_DFR(x, 0, 0),
+			};
+			struct spi_transfer xfer = {
+				.tx_buf = &bootstrap,
+				.rx_buf = &bootstrap,
+				.len    = sizeof(bootstrap),
+			};
+			struct spi_message m;
+
+			spi_message_init_with_transfers(&m, &xfer, 1);
+			spi_sync(spi, &m);
+		}
+	}
 
 	err = devm_device_add_group(dev, &ads784x_attr_group);
 	if (err)
--
2.43.0
